window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>If it weren’t for bad luck, she’d have no luck at all. <br> <br> Ekko Rose is no stranger to struggle. Born to a single, addicted mother, she’s experienced more than her fair share of hardship. Ekko has dreams she’s desperate to fulfill, but when another stroke of bad luck leaves her homeless, her only option is to focus on survival. <br> <br> Dominick \"Dom\" Moore has had his eyes on Ekko ever since he saved her life several months ago. He kept his distance then because she was attached to another man. Now, seeing her living out of her car, Dom resolves to help her get back on her feet. <br> <br> When Dom approaches Ekko, she wrestles with knowing her rightful place in the world and wanting to latch onto something better. <br> <br> Just as the pair fall hard for one another, Ekko’s streak of misfortune delivers one more blow. With their relationship thrown into a pit of despair and hopeless desire, Dom must crack the case he’s been trying to solve for weeks. <br> <br> Because if he can’t, Ekko might be lost to him forever. </p>"; 
